"| before | after                |\n"
"|:------------ |:----------------------- |\n"
"| §1    | §2 and §3         |\n"
"| §4    | §5 and §6 |\n"
"\n"
"## Friends and relatives\n"
"\n"
"* You can break down an *assumption* into its components using §7.\n"
"* If you want to prove §8, you have to choose one side using §9 or §10."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `contradiction`
#. §1: `h : n ≠ n`
#. §2: `h : A`
#. §3: `h' : ¬A`
#. §4: `h : False`
#. §5: `contradiction`
#. §6: `by_contra`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:114
msgid "The tactic §0 concludes the proof if it finds a contradiction in the assumptions.\n"
"Such a contradiction can look like this, for example:\n"
"\n"
"* §1\n"
"* §2 and §3\n"
"* §4\n"
"\n"
"## Friends and relatives\n"
"\n"
"Normally, §5 is used to conclude a proof by contradiction\n"
"that was opened with §6."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `contrapose`
#. §1: `A → B`
#. §2: `¬B → ¬A`
#. §3: `revert h`
#. §4: `contrapose`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:129
msgid "The tactic §0 changes a proof goal of the form §1 to §2, thereby\n"
"initiating a proof by contraposition.\n"
"\n"
"## Friends and relatives\n"
"\n"
"The tactic §3 can be useful for writing an assumption as an implication premise\n"
"before you use §4."
msgstr ""

#. §0: ```
#. A = B
#. ```
#. §1: `T`
#. §2: `A B : Set T`
#. §3: `ext x`
#. §4: ```
#. x ∈ A ↔ x ∈ B
#. ```
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:146
msgid "Two subsets of a given set are equal if they have the same elements.\n"
"If the proof goal is\n"
"§0\n"
"for two subsets of §1 (i.e., for §2),\n"
"then §3 converts the proof goal into the equivalence\n"
"§4"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `fin_cases i`
#. §1: `i`
#. §2: `fin_cases i`
#. §3: `(i : Fin n)`
#. §4: `fin_cases i`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:160
msgid "§0 führt eine Fallunterscheidung, wenn §1 ein endlicher Typ ist.\n"
"\n"
"## Details\n"
"§2 ist insbesondere nützlich für §3, zum Beispiel als Index in\n"
"endlich dimensionalen Vektorräumen.\n"
"\n"
"In diesem Fall bewirkt §4, dass du komponentenweise arbeitest."
msgstr ""

#. §0: ```
#. f = g
#. ```
#. §1: `f g : X → Y`
#. §2: `funext x`
#. §3: ```
#. f x = g x
#. ```
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:171
msgid "Two mappings with the same range and domain are equal if\n"
"they take the same values on all elements of the domain.\n"
"A proof goal of the form\n"
"§0\n"
"for mappings §1 is converted by §2\n"
"into the equation\n"
"§3."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `generalize`
#. §1: `generalize h : a = b`
#. §2: `a`
#. §3: `b`
#. §4: `h : a = b`
#. §5: ```
#. Even x ∨ ¬Even x
#. ```
#. §6: ```
#. generalize h : (Even x) = A
#. ```
#. §7: ```
#. A ∨ ¬A
#. ```
#. §8: `tauto`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:186
msgid "With §0, you can generalize a proof goal\n"
"in the hope that a higher level of abstraction will allow for a simpler proof.\n"
"More precisely, §1 replaces all occurrences of §2 in the proof goal with §3\n"
"(and adds the assumption §4).\n"
"\n"
"## Example\n"
"\n"
"A goal of the form\n"
"§5\n"
"can be converted with\n"
"§6\n"
"into\n"
"§7\n"
"(and then simply proven with §8)."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `grind`
#. §1: `grind [h₁, h₂]`
#. §2: `h₁`
#. §3: `h₂`
#. §4: `@[grind]`
#. §5: `grind only [h₁, h₂]`
#. §6: `simp`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:210
msgid "The §0 tactic is a powerful automation tactic.\n"
"It tries to close the proof goal by combining several techniques,\n"
"including case splitting, congruence closure, and arithmetic reasoning.\n"
"It can often finish goals that would otherwise require several manual steps.\n"
"\n"
"## Variants\n"
"\n"
"* §1 uses the assumptions or lemmas §2 and §3\n"
"    in addition to lemmas marked with §4 in mathlib\n"
"* §5 exclusively uses the given lemmas\n"
"\n"
"## Friends and relatives\n"
"\n"
"* §6 simplifies the goal step by step using rewrite lemmas,\n"
"  but does not perform case splits."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `have h : P`
#. §1: `suffices h : P`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:229
msgid "With §0, you introduce an intermediate result.\n"
"You must then prove this intermediate result\n"
"before you can continue with the actual proof.\n"
"\n"
"## Related\n"
"§1 works in exactly the same way, except that you can continue with the main proof first and\n"
"only have to prove your intermediate result at the very end."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `if … then … else`
#. §1: `fun x ↦ if 0 ≤ x then x else -x`
#. §2: `h : A`
#. §3: `rw [if_pos h]`
#. §4: `if A then B else C`
#. §5: `B`
#. §6: `h : ¬ A`
#. §7: `rw [if_neg h]`
#. §8: `if A then B else C`
#. §9: `C`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:244
msgid "With §0, you can define mappings with two branches of definition.\n"
"\n"
"For example, §1 defines the absolute value function.\n"
"\n"
"## Friends and relatives\n"
"\n"
"* If you have §2 as an assumption, you can use\n"
"§3 to reduce the expression §4 to §5.\n"
"* If you have §6 as an assumption, you can use\n"
"§7 to reduce the expression §8 to §9."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `induction n`
#. §1: `n`
#. §2: `induction n with d dh`
#. §3: `d`
#. §4: `hd`
#. §5: `n = 0`
#. §6: `hd`
#. §7: `induction`
#. §8: `induction'`
#. §9: `0`
#. §10: `Nat.zero`
#. §11: `d + 1`
#. §12: `Nat.succ d`
#. §13: `zero_eq`
#. §14: `Nat.succ_eq_add_one`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:258
msgid "The tactic §0 performs an inductive proof over §1.\n"
"With §2, you can specify names for the induction variable (here: §3)\n"
"and the induction assumption (here: §4).\n"
"The tactic thus replaces the original proof goal with two new proof goals:\n"
"* an induction start, in which §5 is set, and\n"
"* an induction step, in which the induction assumption §6 is available to you.\n"
"\n"
"## Modifications in this game\n"
"\n"
"Outside of this game, §7 is called §8,\n"
"§9 is initially written as §10 and §11 as §12.\n"
"These terms are identical in definition, but occasionally need to be explicitly rewritten with\n"
"§13 and §14."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `intro`
#. §1: `A → B`
#. §2: `∀ x, P x`
#. §3: `A → B`
#. §4: `intro h`
#. §5: `h : A`
#. §6: `B`
#. §7: `∀ x, P x`
#. §8: `intro x`
#. §9: `x`
#. §10: `P x`
#. §11: `⊢ A → B`
#. §12: `intro h`
#. §13: `h : A`
#. §14: `⊢ B`
#. §15: `⊢  x, P x`
#. §16: `intro x hx`
#. §17: `x : X`
#. §18: `hx : P x`
#. §19: `⊢ P x`
#. §20: `revert h`
#. §21: `intro h`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:296
msgid "The tactic §0 is used for   proof goals of the form §1 or §2.\n"
"\n"
"If your proof goal is §3, §4 gives you the assumption §5, and you then have to prove §6.\n"
"If your proof goal is §7, §8 gices you an arbitrary §9 and you have to prove §10.\n"
"\n"
"| before | tactic       | after                     |\n"
"|:------------ |:------------ |:---------------------------- |\n"
"| §11    | §12    | §13, §14               |\n"
"| §15  | §16 | §17, §18, §19 |\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"## Friends and relatives\n"
"\n"
"The tactic §20 does the exact opposite of §21."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A ∨ B`
#. §1: `left`
#. §2: `right`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:314
msgid "If the proof target is of the form §0, you choose §1 to show the left side.\n"
"\n"
"## Friends and relatives\n"
"\n"
"With §2, you choose the right side accordingly."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `let`
#. §1: `let x : ℕ := 5 ^ 2`
#. §2: `let x := …`
#. §3: `x`
#. §4: `simp only [x]`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:323
msgid "The §0 tactic introduces a temporary definition, for example\n"
"§1.\n"
"\n"
"Once §2 defines a §3, you can use the definition later with §4."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `linarith`
#. §1: ```
#. h : m ≤ x → n < x
#. ```
#. §2: ```
#. rw [imp_iff_or_not] at h
#. ```
#. §3: ```
#. h : n < x ∨ ¬m ≤ x
#. ```
#. §4: `linarith`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:343
msgid "The tactic §0 can show that a linear equation or inequality follows from given equations or inequalities.\n"
"It is quite flexible and works just as well in ℕ as in ℝ.\n"
"However, the (in)equations must be given individually, not logically linked.\n"
"An assumption of the form\n"
"§1\n"
"must first be rewritten with\n"
"§2\n"
"to\n"
"§3\n"
"so that §4 can do something with it."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `omega`
#. §1: `ℕ`
#. §2: `ℤ`
#. §3: `linarith`
#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:363
msgid "The tactic §0 can show that a linear equation or inequality in §1 or §2\n"
"follows from given equations or inequalities.\n"
"Unlike §3, it can also handle logical connections between (in)equations."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `push Not`
#. §1: `push ¬ _ `
#. §2: `push`
#. §3: `Not`
#. §4: `¬ _`
